  "note": "Triennial election of the electoral divisions of Strabane rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Four divisions were contested: Ballyfatton, Cullion, Douglas and Sion. The other twenty-four councillors were returned unopposed (Strabane Chronicle, 24 May 1952, p. 3, which prints the full list of nominations; labels as printed). Nationalist gain after a recount; Beattie was the outgoing councillor."
